id: 00001012070540
title: API: Metadata key information
role: manual
tags: #api #manual #zettelstore
syntax: zmk
created: 20220304164242
modified: 20261109135645

To retrieve information about metadata keys, send an HTTP GET request to the endpoint ''/x'' with the query parameter ''data=meta-type''.
If [[authentication is enabled|00001010040100]], the caller must be authenticated and must have at least read access.

Without the query parameter ''key'', information about all predefined metadata keys is returned.
The order of the entries is not specified and may differ between requests.

If the query parameter ''key'' is given (possibly more than once), the result contains one entry for each occurrence of ''key'', in the given order.
If the same key is given more than once, the result contains the entry for that key more than once.
An empty value for ''key'' is rejected with status code ''400''.
The type of a key that is not predefined is derived from the suffix of its name, see [[Supported Key Types|00001006030000]].
For example, the key ''data-url'' has the type ''URL''; a key with a suffix not listed there has the type ''EMPTY-STRING''.

````
# curl 'http://127.0.0.1:23123/x?data=meta-type&key=data-url&key=forward'
(("data-url" "URL" () () ()) ("forward" "IdentifierSet" T T T))
````

The result is a list of entries.
Each entry is a list of five elements, in this order:
# The name of the key, in its string representation.
# The name of the type of the key, in its string representation, see [[Supported Key Types|00001006030000]].
# ''T'', if the type is a set type, i.e. the value is a set of elements, otherwise ''()''.
# ''T'', if the value of the key is computed by Zettelstore, otherwise ''()''.
  A computed value may be stored in the zettel, and the stored value is used.
  If it is not stored, Zettelstore computes it and may update the zettel, so that the value becomes persistent.
# ''T'', if the value of the key is a property, otherwise ''()''.

A property is always computed by Zettelstore, even if a value is stored in the zettel; the stored value is ignored.
Every property is also computed, but a computed value is not necessarily a property.
See [[Supported Metadata Keys|00001006020000]] for the keys that are properties or computed.

==== HTTP Status codes
; ''200''
: Retrieval was successful, the body contains the list.
; ''400''
: The value of the query parameter ''key'' is empty.
; ''403''
: Authentication is enabled, and the caller is not authenticated or does not have read access.